From 9f1b0803de545065cefb9992d99f9362ccb94596 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 13:19:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(walkthrough): data-driven schematic spec + fuel-system
 layout for P0087
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the hard-coded engine-bay Canvas with a generic SchematicRenderer
that consumes a per-DTC SchematicSpec. The renderer walks a declarative
list of shapes and overlays accent regions for any highlighted ID, so
adding a new DTC family is one data file (no Canvas math). Ships:

- SchematicSpec + SchematicShape sealed types under ui/components/schematic
- EngineBaySchematic — coordinates lifted verbatim from EngineDiagram so
  P0301 renders the same shape
- FuelSystemSchematic — new diesel common-rail layout (tank → filter →
  primer bulb → HP pump → rail → injectors) so P0087 finally has a
  relevant diagram
- Aesthetic polish inside the renderer: faint background grid, inner
  bezel, highlight-alpha pulse (1.5s reverse, matches the loading-page
  dots), shadow-layered label text for legibility
- DiagramTarget enum → DiagramTargets string constants so new targets
  (FUEL_FILTER, PRIMER_BULB, FUEL_RAIL) extend without enum churn;
  highlightsForPlanStep gains filter/prime/rail/pressure keywords
- WalkthroughScreen hides the diagram card entirely when schematic is
  null (P0171, P0118) instead of showing an irrelevant engine bay

P0301 should render identically apart from the pulse/grid; P0087 now
shows a fuel-system diagram driven by the same step keyword matcher.

